IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc5-s118-to-130-1.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: PART IV Offences Against the Administration of Law and Justice,
-- the definitions of section 118 and the sub-heading "Corruption and Disobedience" (sections 119 to 130.1). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text.
-- Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words;
-- NOTHING where it does not (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc5)"). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Section 2 terms the offences turn on are INPUTS typed MAYBE BOOLEAN, named `s 2 <term>: ...` (PLAN.md section 4).

§ `Part IV -- Interpretation: section 118 ("In this Part")`

-- src:2715 | evidence or statement means an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge, whether material or not and whether admissible or not; (témoignage, déposition ou déclaration)
@ref s 118 "evidence or statement" (src:2715)
GIVEN `the thing is an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assertion is material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assertion is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 evidence or statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge"


-- government means (a) the Government of Canada, (b) the government of a province, or (c) Her Majesty in right of Canada or a province.
-- src:2716 | government means
-- src:2717 | (a) the Government of Canada,
-- src:2718 | (b) the government of a province, or
-- src:2719 | (c) Her Majesty in right of Canada or a province; (gouvernement)
@ref s 118 "government" (src:2716-2719)
DECLARE `s 118 body` IS ONE OF
    `s 118(a) the Government of Canada`
    `s 118(b) the government of a province`
    `s 118(c) Her Majesty in right of Canada or a province`
    `s 118 a body not named in the definition of government`

@ref s 118 "government" (src:2716-2719)
GIVEN body IS A `s 118 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 government` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 118(a) the Government of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(b) the government of a province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(c) Her Majesty in right of Canada or a province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118 a body not named in the definition of government` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "government means"


-- judicial proceeding means a proceeding (a) in or under the authority of a court of justice, (b) before the Senate or House of Commons or a committee ... authorized by law to administer an oath,
-- (c) before a court, judge, justice, provincial court judge or coroner, (d) before an arbitrator or umpire, or a person or body ... authorized by law to make an inquiry and take evidence therein under oath,
-- or (e) before a tribunal by which a legal right or legal liability may be established, whether or not the proceeding is invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason.
-- src:2720 | judicial proceeding means a proceeding
-- src:2721 | (a) in or under the authority of a court of justice,
-- src:2722 | (b) before the Senate or House of Commons or a committee of the Senate or House of Commons, or before a legislative council, legislative assembly or house of assembly or a committee thereof that is authorized by law to administer an oath,
-- src:2723 | (c) before a court, judge, justice, provincial court judge or coroner,
-- src:2724 | (d) before an arbitrator or umpire, or a person or body of persons authorized by law to make an inquiry and take evidence therein under oath, or
-- src:2725 | (e) before a tribunal by which a legal right or legal liability may be established,
-- src:2726 | whether or not the proceeding is invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason; (procédure judiciaire)
@ref s 118 "judicial proceeding" (src:2720-2726)
DECLARE `s 118 forum` IS ONE OF
    `s 118(a) in or under the authority of a court of justice`
    `s 118(b) before the Senate or House of Commons or a committee of either, or before a legislative council, legislative assembly or house of assembly or a committee of it authorized by law to administer an oath`
    `s 118(c) before a court, judge, justice, provincial court judge or coroner`
    `s 118(d) before an arbitrator or umpire, or a person or body of persons authorized by law to make an inquiry and take evidence therein under oath`
    `s 118(e) before a tribunal by which a legal right or legal liability may be established`
    `s 118 before none of those`

@ref s 118 "judicial proceeding" (src:2720-2726)
GIVEN forum IS A `s 118 forum`
      `the proceeding is invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 judicial proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER forum
    WHEN `s 118(a) in or under the authority of a court of justice` THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not invalid: the second input does not change the answer
    WHEN `s 118(b) before the Senate or House of Commons or a committee of either, or before a legislative council, legislative assembly or house of assembly or a committee of it authorized by law to administer an oath` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(c) before a court, judge, justice, provincial court judge or coroner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(d) before an arbitrator or umpire, or a person or body of persons authorized by law to make an inquiry and take evidence therein under oath` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(e) before a tribunal by which a legal right or legal liability may be established` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118 before none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judicial proceeding means a proceeding"


-- office includes (a) an office or appointment under the government, (b) a civil or military commission, and (c) a position or an employment in a public department.
-- src:2727 | office includes
-- src:2728 | (a) an office or appointment under the government,
-- src:2729 | (b) a civil or military commission, and
-- src:2730 | (c) a position or an employment in a public department; (charge ou emploi)
@ref s 118 "office" (src:2727-2730)
DECLARE `s 118 position` IS ONE OF
    `s 118(a) an office or appointment under the government`
    `s 118(b) a civil or military commission`
    `s 118(c) a position or an employment in a public department`
    `s 118 a position that is none of those`

@ref s 118 "office" (src:2727-2730)
GIVEN position IS A `s 118 position`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 office` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 118(a) an office or appointment under the government` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(b) a civil or military commission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118(c) a position or an employment in a public department` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 118 a position that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "office includes"


-- official means a person who (a) holds an office, or (b) is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty.
-- src:2731 | official means a person who
-- src:2732 | (a) holds an office, or
-- src:2733 | (b) is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty; (fonctionnaire)
@ref s 118 "official" (src:2731-2733)
GIVEN `s 118 office: what the person holds is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 official` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 118 office: what the person holds is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 118 office: what the person holds is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "office includes" leaves open whether what the person holds is an office
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "official means a person who"


-- witness means a person who gives evidence orally under oath or by affidavit in a judicial proceeding, whether or not he is competent to be a witness,
-- and includes a child of tender years who gives evidence but does not give it under oath, because, in the opinion of the person presiding, the child does not understand the nature of an oath.
-- src:2734 | witness means a person who gives evidence orally under oath or by affidavit in a judicial proceeding, whether or not he is competent to be a witness, and includes a child of tender years who gives evidence but does not give it under oath, because, in the opinion of the person presiding, the child does not understand the nature of an oath. (témoin)
@ref s 118 "witness" (src:2734)
GIVEN `the person gives evidence orally under oath or by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 118 judicial proceeding: the evidence is given in one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child of tender years who gives evidence but does not give it under oath because, in the opinion of the person presiding, the child does not understand the nature of an oath` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is competent to be a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118 witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person gives evidence orally under oath or by affidavit` AND (`s 118 judicial proceeding: the evidence is given in one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE   -- "whether or not he is competent": the last input does not change the answer
        IF `the person is a child of tender years who gives evidence but does not give it under oath because, in the opinion of the person presiding, the child does not understand the nature of an oath` AND (`s 118 judicial proceeding: the evidence is given in one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE   -- "and includes a child of tender years"
        IF `s 118 judicial proceeding: the evidence is given in one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "judicial proceeding" is itself not settled on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "witness means a person who"

§ `Part IV -- Corruption and Disobedience (ss 119-130.1)`

§§ `s 119 Bribery of judicial officers, etc.`

-- src:2738 | 119 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
-- src:2739 | (a) being the holder of a judicial office, or being a member of Parliament or of the legislature of a province, directly or indirectly, corruptly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, any money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by them in their official capacity, or
@ref s 119(1)(a) (src:2738-2739)
GIVEN `the person is the holder of a judicial office, or a member of Parliament or of the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directly or indirectly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by the person in their official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(a) the holder of a judicial office or legislator corruptly accepts or obtains a benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the holder of a judicial office, or a member of Parliament or of the legislature of a province` AND `the person directly or indirectly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment` AND `the person acts corruptly` AND `the benefit is in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by the person in their official capacity` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2738 | 119 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
-- src:2740 | (b) directly or indirectly, corruptly gives or offers to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person, any money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by that person in their official capacity.
@ref s 119(1)(b) (src:2738-2740)
GIVEN `the person directly or indirectly gives or offers money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift or offer is in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by that person in their official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(b) the person corruptly gives or offers a benefit to a judicial officer or legislator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person directly or indirectly gives or offers money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person` AND `the person acts corruptly` AND `the gift or offer is in respect of anything done or omitted or to be done or omitted by that person in their official capacity` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2738 | 119 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
@ref s 119(1) (src:2738)
GIVEN `the answer of s 119(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 119(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1) the person is guilty of an indictable offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 119(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 119(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section reaches only the conduct its paragraphs describe

-- src:2738 | 119 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
@ref s 119(1) (src:2738)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 119(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:2738 | 119 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
@ref s 119(1) (src:2738)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 119(1) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no minimum
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

-- src:2742 | (2) No proceedings against a person who holds a judicial office shall be instituted under this section without the consent in writing of the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 119(2) (src:2742)
GIVEN `the proceedings are instituted under section 119` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person against whom they are instituted holds a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(2) the proceedings against a holder of a judicial office are barred for want of the written consent of the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented in writing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the consent in writing of the Attorney General of Canada"
        IF `the proceedings are instituted under section 119` AND `the person against whom they are instituted holds a judicial office` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `s 120 Bribery of officers`

-- src:2744 | 120 Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
-- src:2745 | (a) being a justice, police commissioner, peace officer, public officer or officer of a juvenile court, or being employed in the administration of criminal law, directly or indirectly, corruptly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, any money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment with intent
-- src:2746 | (i) to interfere with the administration of justice,
-- src:2747 | (ii) to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence, or
-- src:2748 | (iii) to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed or who intends to commit an offence; or
@ref s 120(a) (src:2744-2748)
GIVEN `s 2 justice: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a police commissioner or an officer of a juvenile court, or is employed in the administration of criminal law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directly or indirectly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to interfere with the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed or who intends to commit an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120(a) the officer or person employed in the administration of criminal law corruptly accepts or obtains a benefit with a stated intent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`s 2 justice: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 2 public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is a police commissioner or an officer of a juvenile court, or is employed in the administration of criminal law`) AND `the person directly or indirectly accepts, obtains, agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, for themselves or another person, money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment` AND `the person acts corruptly` AND (`the person acts with intent to interfere with the administration of justice` OR `the person acts with intent to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` OR `the person acts with intent to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed or who intends to commit an offence`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2744 | 120 Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years who
-- src:2749 | (b) directly or indirectly, corruptly gives or offers to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person, any money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment with intent that the person should do anything mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii).
@ref s 120(b) (src:2744-2749)
GIVEN `the person directly or indirectly gives or offers money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent that the officer should interfere with the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent that the officer should procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent that the officer should protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed or who intends to commit an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120(b) the person corruptly gives or offers a benefit to an officer with a stated intent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person directly or indirectly gives or offers money, valuable consideration, office, place or employment to a person mentioned in paragraph (a), or to anyone for the benefit of that person` AND `the person acts corruptly` AND (`the person acts with intent that the officer should interfere with the administration of justice` OR `the person acts with intent that the officer should procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` OR `the person acts with intent that the officer should protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed or who intends to commit an offence`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

