§§ `s 121 Frauds on the government`

-- src:2751 | 121 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:2752 | (a) directly or indirectly
-- src:2753 | (i) gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an official or to any member of his family, or to any one for the benefit of an official, or
-- src:2754 | (ii) being an official, demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person for himself or another person,
-- src:2755 | a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission in connection with
-- src:2756 | (iii) the transaction of business with or any matter of business relating to the government, or
-- src:2757 | (iv) a claim against Her Majesty or any benefit that Her Majesty is authorized or is entitled to bestow,
-- src:2758 | whether or not, in fact, the official is able to cooperate, render assistance, exercise influence or do or omit to do what is proposed, as the case may be;
@ref s 121(1)(a) (src:2751-2758)
GIVEN `s 118 official: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person directly or indirectly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an official or to a member of an official's family, or to anyone for the benefit of an official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, being an official, directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person for themselves or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is given or received is a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or received as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with a claim against Her Majesty or any benefit that Her Majesty is authorized or is entitled to bestow` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official is in fact able to cooperate, render assistance, exercise influence or do or omit to do what is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(1)(a) the person gives to an official, or an official takes, a benefit for cooperation or influence in government business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 118 official: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the person directly or indirectly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an official or to a member of an official's family, or to anyone for the benefit of an official` OR `the person, being an official, directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person for themselves or another person`) AND `what is given or received is a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` AND `it is given or received as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission` AND (`in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` OR `in connection with a claim against Her Majesty or any benefit that Her Majesty is authorized or is entitled to bestow`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2751 | 121 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:2759 | (b) having dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly pays a commission or reward to or confers an advantage or benefit of any kind on an employee or official of the government with which the dealings take place, or to any member of the employee’s or official’s family, or to anyone for the benefit of the employee or official, with respect to those dealings, unless the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government with which the dealings take place;
@ref s 121(1)(b) (src:2751-2759)
GIVEN `the person has dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person pays a commission or reward to, or confers an advantage or benefit of any kind on, an employee or official of the government with which the dealings take place, or a member of that person's family, or anyone for that person's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with respect to those dealings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government with which the dealings take place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(1)(b) the person having dealings with the government pays or confers a benefit on its employee or official without written consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government with which the dealings take place` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government with which the dealings take place"
        IF `the person has dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly` AND `the person pays a commission or reward to, or confers an advantage or benefit of any kind on, an employee or official of the government with which the dealings take place, or a member of that person's family, or anyone for that person's benefit` AND `it is with respect to those dealings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2751 | 121 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:2760 | (c) being an official or employee of the government, directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from a person who has dealings with the government a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind for themselves or another person, unless they have the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government that employs them or of which they are an official;
@ref s 121(1)(c) (src:2751-2760)
GIVEN `the person is an official or employee of the government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind for themselves or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is from a person who has dealings with the government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government that employs them or of which they are an official` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(1)(c) the official or employee of the government takes a benefit from a person dealing with it without written consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government that employs them or of which they are an official` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have the consent in writing of the head of the branch of government that employs them or of which they are an official"
        IF `the person is an official or employee of the government` AND `the person directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind for themselves or another person` AND `it is from a person who has dealings with the government` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2751 | 121 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:2761 | (d) having or pretending to have influence with the government or with a minister of the government or an official, directly or indirectly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept, for themselves or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission in connection with
-- src:2762 | (i) anything mentioned in subparagraph (a)(iii) or (iv), or
-- src:2763 | (ii) the appointment of any person, including themselves, to an office;
@ref s 121(1)(d) (src:2751-2763)
GIVEN `the person has, or pretends to have, influence with the government, a minister of the government or an official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directly or indirectly demands, accepts, or offers or agrees to accept, for themselves or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with a claim against Her Majesty or any benefit that Her Majesty is authorized or is entitled to bestow` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with the appointment of any person, including themselves, to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(1)(d) the person with, or pretending to have, influence demands or accepts a reward for it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has, or pretends to have, influence with the government, a minister of the government or an official` AND `the person directly or indirectly demands, accepts, or offers or agrees to accept, for themselves or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` AND `it is as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence or an act or omission` AND (`in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` OR `in connection with a claim against Her Majesty or any benefit that Her Majesty is authorized or is entitled to bestow` OR `in connection with the appointment of any person, including themselves, to an office`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

