      `the person holds an office under a municipal government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(3) municipal official` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is a member of a municipal council` OR `the person holds an office under a municipal government`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a member of a municipal council or a person who holds an office under a municipal government"

